==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*varis}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*warᴈ}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|vares}}, {{cog|vep|variš}}, {{cog|krl|varis}}, {{cog|myv|варака}}, {{cog|mdf|варси}} and {{cog|hu|varjú}}. Likely an onomatopoeic word, compare {{noncog|ru|воро́на}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[hooded crow]], [[grey crow]], {{taxfmt|Corvus cornix|species}}
# [[corvid]], [[crow]] {{gloss|any bird of the genus ''Corvus''}}

====Usage notes====
Until recently [[carrion crow]] ({{m|fi|nokivaris}}, which is rarely seen in Finland but common in England) was believed to be just a black variant of [[hooded crow]] or [[grey crow]] (which is common in Finland but less common in England). Therefore many dictionaries give "carrion crow" as translation for {{m|fi||varis}}.

